# Canyon Crab: "At the beginning of your end step, if you haven't cast a spell from your hand this turn, draw a card, then discard
# a card." Bot1 casts the Crab from their hand on turn one, so nothing triggers at that end step. On turn three they cast nothing:
# the trigger goes on the stack, draws the Plains on top of the library, and Bot1 discards the Forest drawn for the turn (a card
# that was already in hand), keeping the Plains: hand and graveyard each change by that one card.

[Bot1 Deck]
Canyon Crab
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Island x4
Forest
Plains
Island x8

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Canyon Crab.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T1 Bot1.End]
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 4
[T3 Bot1.End]
? Stack.Count = 1
? Bot1.Hand = Forest; Island; Island; Island; Island
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Forest)

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Forest
Bot1.Hand = Island; Island; Island; Island; Plains
